  "reason": "The strongest completed result is RNA-only PCA singleprofile (0.485 acc), while image-only models are much weaker (0.21-0.23 acc), so RNA representation is the promising direction. The key uncertainty is whether using multiple profiles with a simple aggregation improves on the singleprofile RNA baseline. config_002 keeps the same RNA encoder and modality, changing only to multiprofile with avgpool, making it a clean test of profile setting/aggregation. It is a better use of the next budget than adding fusion or changing multiple factors, because it directly clarifies whether multiprofile aggregation is worth pursuing before more complex RNA or multimodal variants."
